@startuml
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam backgroundColor #fcfcfd
skinparam defaultFontName Helvetica
skinparam defaultFontSize 14
skinparam arrowColor #0f172a
skinparam noteBackgroundColor #fff7d6
skinparam noteBorderColor #b45309
skinparam noteFontColor #334155
skinparam roundcorner 16
title State Machine - generativeaiagent/DataSource
skinparam state {
  backgroundColor #f8fafc
  borderColor #0f172a
  fontColor #0f172a
  startColor #1d4ed8
  endColor #0f172a
}
left to right direction
hide empty description
state "Observe" as observe
state "EvaluateReady" as evaluate_ready
state "Ready" as ready
state "Retryable" as retryable
state "Failed" as failed
observe : read spec, tracked status, delete intent,\nand current OCI lifecycle
state "ResolveByLookup" as resolve_by_lookup
state "RejectUnsupportedDrift" as reject_unsupported_drift
state "ApplyUpdate" as apply_update
state "DeletePending" as delete_pending
state "Deleted" as deleted
state "DeleteCleanupBlocked" as delete_cleanup_blocked
[*] --> observe : CreateDataSource
observe --> resolve_by_lookup : tracked identity missing
resolve_by_lookup --> evaluate_ready : lookup or create reaches\nACTIVE, INACTIVE
resolve_by_lookup --> retryable : OCI state in CREATING,\nUPDATING, DELETING
resolve_by_lookup --> failed : unresolved OCI error or non-success state
observe --> evaluate_ready : OCI state in ACTIVE,\nINACTIVE
observe --> retryable : OCI state in CREATING,\nUPDATING, DELETING
observe --> failed : unresolved OCI error or non-success state
evaluate_ready --> reject_unsupported_drift : force-new or conflicting\ndrift detected
reject_unsupported_drift --> ready : wait for spec or live state change
evaluate_ready --> apply_update : supported mutable drift for\ndataSourceConfig,\ndefinedTags, description (+3\nmore)
apply_update --> ready : update path completes
evaluate_ready --> ready : no supported drift remains
ready --> ready : no supported drift remains
retryable --> retryable : OCI remains retryable
failed --> failed : OCI remains terminal
ready --> delete_pending : delete requested
retryable --> delete_pending : delete requested
failed --> delete_pending : delete requested
delete_pending --> delete_cleanup_blocked : cleanup or finalizer release remains blocked
delete_cleanup_blocked --> deleted : retry delete completion until allowed
deleted --> deleted : terminal stutter
note right of ready
shared diagram:
shared/diagrams/shared-controller-state-machine.svg
Start from the shared controller phase model and
specialize imported provider states, delete
targets, and failure exits here.
archetype batch: Generated service-manager
controllers map provider states into the shared
controller phases with explicit finalizer and
requeue policies.
service: generativeaiagent
slug: datasource
kind: DataSource
archetype: generated-service-manager
status/finalizer: required /
retain-until-confirmed-delete
requeue: provisioning, updating, terminating
provider states: create CREATING; update
UPDATING; delete DELETING
follow-up: create=GetWorkRequest ->
GetDataSource; update=GetWorkRequest ->
GetDataSource; delete=GetWorkRequest ->
GetDataSource/ListDataSources confirm-delete
supported drift: dataSourceConfig, definedTags,
description, displayName (+2 more)
reject before mutate: force-new fields
compartmentId, knowledgeBaseId
create-only fields: none
list lookup:
oci_generative_ai_agent_data_sources filters
compartmentId, knowledgeBaseId, displayName;
exact compartmentId plus knowledgeBaseId plus
displayName unique match in ACTIVE, INACTIVE,
CREATING, or UPDATING; duplicate matches fail
conflicts: none
open gaps: none
Reviewed lifecycle mapping treats CREATING as
provisioning, UPDATING as updating, ACTIVE and
INACTIVE as success, and DELETING as
terminating; FAILED is terminal and DELETED is
only a delete-confirmation target.
CreateDataSource returns a DataSource body plus
opc-work-request-id, while UpdateDataSource and
DeleteDataSource return work-request headers
without a resource body. The runtime prefers the
create response identifier and otherwise
recovers the DataSource OCID from work-request
resources before rereading GetDataSource.
Pre-create reuse only runs when spec.displayName
is present and keeps exact compartmentId plus
knowledgeBaseId plus displayName matching
bounded to ACTIVE, INACTIVE, CREATING, or
UPDATING summaries.
Only displayName, description, dataSourceConfig,
metadata, freeformTags, and definedTags
reconcile in place; compartmentId and
knowledgeBaseId remain replacement-only.
Delete keeps the finalizer until the work
request is terminal and GetDataSource or
fallback ListDataSources confirms the resource
is gone.
Shared manifest promotion for this row is
intentionally deferred to the convergence story.
end note
note right of delete_pending
delete policy: required
delete observe: GetDataSource or ListDataSources
delete targets: DELETED
end note
@enduml
